atients negative for minimal residual disease. Numbers are for patients positive for minimal residual disease, with complete remission.</p></fn><fn id="tfn8-co14_3p096"><label>e</label><p>Regimen details not reported.</p></fn><fn id="tfn9-co14_3p096"><label>f</label><p>Alemtuzumab administered intravenously twice weekly for up to 8 weeks, plus rituximab (375 mg/m<sup>2</sup>) administered weekly for 4 weeks. <sc>or</sc> = overall response rate; <sc>cr</sc> = complete response; <sc>pr</sc> = partial response; <sc>ttp</sc> = time to progression; pts. = patients; <sc>os</sc> = overall survival; abs. = abstract; <sc>nr</sc> = not reported; <sc>cfar</sc> = cyclophosphamide 250 mg/m<sup>2</sup> days 3&#x02013;5, fludarabine 25 mg/m<sup>2</sup> days 3&#x02013;5, alemtuzumab 30 mg days 1, 3, 5, rituximab 375&#x02013;500 mg/m<sup>2</sup> day 2.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tIII-co14_3p096" position="float"><label>TABLE III</label><caption><p>Responses to maintenance or consolidation therapy (or both): randomized and single-arm trials of alemtuzumab for chronic lymphocytic leukemia (<sc>cll</sc>)</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Reference</italic></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic><sc>cll</sc></italic><italic>population</italic></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Intervention</italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn10-co14_3p096">a</xref></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Patients [</italic>N <italic>(</italic>n<italic>)]</italic><xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tfn11-co14_3p096">b</xref></th><th colspan="2" align="center" rowspan="1"><italic>Post-induction</italic></th><th colspan="2" align="center" rowspan="1"><italic>Post-alemtuzumab</italic></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Median</italic></th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Median</italic></th></tr><tr><th align="left"